sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as Client<br/>(Web / Mobile)
    participant LB as Load Balancer
    participant MS as Microservice<br/>(Container)
    participant Outbox as Outbox Table<br/>(in MS DB)
    participant Kafka as Kafka Broker<br/>(Event Stream)
    participant DB as Database<br/>(Final State)

    Client->>LB: HTTP Request
    LB->>MS: Route Request
    MS->>Outbox: Write Event to Outbox Table<br/>(Transactional)
    Note right of MS: Ensures atomic write<br/>to DB + Outbox
    MS-->>Client: HTTP 202 Accepted<br/>(Async Processing)
    
    loop Outbox Poller / CDC
        MS->>Kafka: Publish Event from Outbox<br/>(via Poller or Debezium CDC)
        Kafka->>Kafka: Persist Event
    end

    Kafka->>DB: Consumer Service Applies Event<br/>(Idempotent Update)
    Note right of DB: Eventually Consistent<br/>Final State Updated

    Note over Client,DB: All services containerized,<br/>orchestrated via Kubernetes or Docker Compose